## 1. Verified KPI Targets

Goal: Reduce delays in the loan assessment process while ensuring timely final decisions and optimizing loan officer workload without causing overload.

  1. Average Loan Assessment Cycle Time [time] — minimize (scope: end_to_end)
  2. Average Wait Time Before Assessment Start [time] — minimize (scope: activity_level)
  3. Loan Officer Workload Utilization [utilization] — minimize (scope: end_to_end)

Reasoning: This KPI set aligns with the simulation goal by focusing on reducing delays in the loan assessment process while optimizing loan officer workload. The average loan assessment cycle time and average wait time before approval directly target the goal of reducing delays, while the loan officer workload utilization KPI ensures that staff are effectively utilized without being overloaded. The new KPI, Average Wait Time Before Assessment Start, specifically addresses the expert's concern about delays after background checks are completed. All KPIs are measurable based on the provided event log evidence.

These KPIs have been human-verified. Minimize/maximize KPIs are your optimisation targets. Maintain KPIs are constraints — your scenario must not degrade them.

